The extractor requires a literal `r-scripts/<name>.R` in the verify file. My verify file builds the path with `file.path("r-scripts", "bayesian_era_mediation.R")` → no match → ERA treated as unvalidated.

Fix in the test's extractor (more robust, keeps engine code clean): also accept `file.path("r-scripts", "x.R")` and `"r-scripts" / "x.R"`. Plus fix the tautological else-branch check into a real one.

Also: since validatedEngines drives a branch, this bug meant the ERA engine's 40-item acceptance was invisible to home status.

Let me patch:
```js
const validatedEngines = new Set(
  fs.readdirSync(...).filter(...).flatMap((f) => {
    const src = read(`r-scripts/tools/${f}`);
    const lit = (src.match(/r-scripts\/([a-z0-9_]+\.R)/g) || []).map((x) => x.split('/')[1]);
    // 也认 R 里常见的 file.path("r-scripts", "x.R") 写法：上一版只认字面路径，
    // 于是 verify_era_engine.R 明明验收了引擎，首页那边却当成"没人验收过"。
    const joined = (src.match(/file\.path\(\s*"r-scripts"\s*,\s*"([a-z0-9_]+\.R)"/g) || [])
      .map((x) => (x.match(/"([a-z0-9_]+\.R)"/) || [])[1]);
    return [...lit, ...joined.filter(Boolean)];
  })
);
```
And the else-branch assertion → real:
```js
