Structure ✓ I can add a computed `powerHint()` returning a message when n is between 6 and 19 (功效低 ✓) or n<6 (会被拒 ✓) — and render it as a hint under the run button ✓ (but not blocking ✓ since n≥6 is enforced by the engine ✓)

Implementation:
```js
// computed
powerHint() {
  const n = Number(this.permanovaMedParams.mediatorN ?? this.refSampleN('outcomeDataStr') ?? 0);
  if (!n || n < 6) return '';              // 引擎会明确拒单，提示由错误信息承担
  if (n < 15) return `当前样本数 n=${n}：中介检验功效很低，即使真有效应也很可能报不显著（建议 n≥20）`;
  if (n < 20) return `当前样本数 n=${n}：可以跑，但 n<20 的间接效应区间通常偏宽（建议 n≥20）`;
  return '';
}
```
Template: after the run button ✓ add
```html
<span v-if="powerHint" class="run-hint power-hint"> ... {{ powerHint }}</span>
```
Careful: the existing `run-hint` shows when !canRunAnalysis ✓ so mine should be `v-if="powerHint && canRunAnalysis"` ✓ so they don't collide ✓

Then test_med_view assertion: powerHint computed exists ✓ returns '' for n=60 ✓ returns text for n=10 ✓ ✓ (test_med_view has a vm harness ✓)

Let me implement both ✓

